## Engineering workflow (AI-DLC)

For any non-trivial software work (a project, service, multi-file feature, schema change, anything
touching auth, secrets, payments, PII or untrusted input), follow `.agents/skills/ai-dlc-engineering/SKILL.md`
(adjust the path if the skill lives elsewhere). In short:

1. State the tier (see `references/tiers.md`). Tier 0 and 1 work skips the ceremony.
2. Run `python <skill-dir>/scripts/aidlc.py status` and `next`. Resume from `.aidlc/` if it exists.
3. Clarify once in a batch, then write requirements, architecture, a threat model and a milestone plan.
4. Stop and wait for my explicit approval at every gate (G1, G2, G3, G4 per milestone, G5). Silence or
   enthusiasm is not approval. Never approve on my behalf.
5. Build one milestone at a time, tests first. Run the tests yourself and show real command output.
6. Never weaken, skip or delete a test to make it pass. Never claim something works without running it.
7. Change `.aidlc/` only through `aidlc.py`, never by hand.
